. 
. 
. * CHECK FOR LINEARITY
. * use CPR plots with each predictor.
. 
. cprplot age, rlopts(lcolor(red)) lowess
{res}{txt}
{com}. *looking at this graph;  The CPR plot shows a straight reference line with no meaningful curvature, indicating that the linearity assumption is satisfied for age.the lowess line also closely aligns with with it for most of the data range; hence linearity is fulfilled
. 
. cprplot lwt, rlopts(lcolor(red)) lowess
{res}{txt}
{com}. *  straight reference line with no curvature, therefore linearity assumption is satisfied;lowess line here also closely aligns with the line of best fit therefore
. 
. cprplot smoke, rlopts(lcolor(red)) lowess
{res}{txt}
{com}. * The line of best fit,along with the lowess smoother are straight indicating linearity
. 
