{p 0 11 0}Variable:{space 1}{res:ht}{p_end}

H0: Constant variance

{ralign 11:chi2({res:1})} = {res}{ralign 6:0.55}
{txt}{ralign 11:Prob > chi2} = {res}{ralign 6:0.4563}
{txt}
{com}. estat hettest ui

{txt}Breusch–Pagan/Cook–Weisberg test for heteroskedasticity 
Assumption: Normal error terms
{p 0 11 0}Variable:{space 1}{res:ui}{p_end}

H0: Constant variance

{ralign 11:chi2({res:1})} = {res}{ralign 6:0.95}
{txt}{ralign 11:Prob > chi2} = {res}{ralign 6:0.3300}
{txt}
{com}. estat hettest ftv2

{txt}Breusch–Pagan/Cook–Weisberg test for heteroskedasticity 
Assumption: Normal error terms
{p 0 11 0}Variable:{space 1}{res:ftv2}{p_end}

H0: Constant variance

{ralign 11:chi2({res:1})} = {res}{ralign 6:0.06}
{txt}{ralign 11:Prob > chi2} = {res}{ralign 6:0.8077}
{txt}
{com}. 
. *Though the age-specific Breusch-Pagan / Cook-Weisberg test for age is signficant, the overall test is non signficant and the RVP plot for age looked rectangular; therefore the  assumption of equal variance in model is considered met.
. 
. 
